        <div class="prose">
          <h2>A commuter town at a motorway crossroads</h2>
          <p>A large share of West Bromwich's residents commute into <a href="birmingham.html">Birmingham</a> and around the Black Country each day, and the town sits directly at the interchange between the M5 and the M6 — one of the busiest junctions in the region. That means a steady rhythm of morning and evening traffic, both on the motorways themselves and on the local roads feeding them. Breakdowns here often follow the commuting pattern — cars that struggle to start on a cold morning before a commute, or vehicles that develop a fault on the drive home. Whether you're stuck on your own street or just about to join the motorway, we'll come to you.</p>

          <h2>Industrial estate call-outs</h2>
          <p>West Bromwich also has a substantial industrial estate, and we're regularly called out to vans and cars parked or working there. As with any industrial or business site, the unit number or company name is useful information, since these estates can have several similar-looking rows of units.</p>

          <h2>Match days at The Hawthorns</h2>
          <p>When West Bromwich Albion are playing at home, the roads around The Hawthorns fill up quickly and side streets that are normally quiet can become hard to move through. If your breakdown happens on or near a match day, let us know — it changes how we plan the route in and where it's realistic to wait.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Broken down near the M5/M6 interchange?</strong> Let us know which motorway you're on and your direction of travel — this is a fast, complex junction, so get well off the running lanes and behind a barrier if you can before calling.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Getting to you</h2>
          <p>West Bromwich sits between <a href="birmingham.html">Birmingham</a> to the east and the wider Black Country to the west, which means a breakdown here can sometimes be described by drivers in terms of one or the other rather than the town itself. That's not a problem — whether you think of yourself as "just off the M5/M6" or "near The Hawthorns," we cover the whole stretch, including the town's residential streets, its industrial estate and the roads connecting them back to the motorway network.</p>
        </div>

